-- title:
--   Connected part of a unipotent p-divisible tower as a formal group
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly $(p)$, and which is complete and separated for the $(p)$-adic filtration. Let $h\in\mathbb N$ and let $L_v$ ($v\in\mathbb N$) be commutative rings that are cocommutative Hopf algebras over $\mathcal O$, finite and free as $\mathcal O$-modules, together with bialgebra maps $t_v\colon L_{v+1}\to L_v$ that are surjective, with $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}L_v=p^{vh}$ and $\ker t_v$ equal to the image of $\ker\varepsilon$ under the $p^v$-fold convolution power of the identity of $L_{v+1}$; assume moreover that for every $v$ the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual of $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v$ (the Cartier dual of the special fibre, with its convolution ring structure) is a local ring. Then there exist $d\in\mathbb N$, a $d$-dimensional commutative formal group law $F$ over $\mathcal O$ (that is, $d$ power series $F_i$ in $2d$ variables with vanishing constant term, linear terms $X_i+Y_i$, associative and symmetric), an integer $h_0\le h$, a second tower $R_{0,v}$ of commutative cocommutative Hopf algebras over $\mathcal O$, finite and free, bialgebra maps $\rho_v\colon L_v\to R_{0,v}$, elements $e_v\in L_v$, bialgebra transitions $t_{0,v}\colon R_{0,v+1}\to R_{0,v}$, and $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\pi_v\colon \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to R_{0,v}$, such that each $t_{0,v}$ is surjective, $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}R_{0,v}=p^{vh_0}$, $\ker t_{0,v}$ is the $p^v$-torsion ideal of $R_{0,v+1}$ (image of $\ker\varepsilon$ under the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity), $\rho_v\circ t_v=t_{0,v}\circ\rho_{v+1}$, $t_{0,v}\circ\pi_{v+1}=\pi_v$, and, for every $v$: $e_v$ is idempotent with $\varepsilon(e_v)=1$; $\rho_v$ is surjective with kernel the ideal $(1-e_v)$; $R_{0,v}$, $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R_{0,v}$ and the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual of the latter are local rings; $\pi_v$ is surjective; each $\pi_v(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)\subseteq R_{0,v}$; $\pi_v$ agrees on every power series with its $(p)$-adic evaluation at the elements $\pi_v(X_i)$; $\ker\pi_v$ is generated by the components of the multiplication-by-$p^v$ series of $F$ (the $p^v$-th iterate $F.\mathtt{nthSeries}$); and $\Delta(\pi_v(X_i))$ equals the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $F_i$ at the elements $\pi_v(X_j)\otimes 1$ and $1\otimes\pi_v(X_j)$ of $R_{0,v}\otimes_{\mathcal O}R_{0,v}$.
--
--   This is the combination of the connected–étale splitting for a $p$-divisible group over $\mathcal O$ (here $\mathcal O=\mathbb Z_p$, presented levelwise through the idempotents $e_v$ cutting out the connected part) with Tate's description of a connected $p$-divisible group as the $p$-power torsion $F[p^\infty]$ of a single commutative formal group law, in coordinates compatible with the whole tower. It is used by [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_connectedComponent_mvFormalGroup_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_connectedComponent_mvFormalGroup_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual), the packaged form of the same assertion.
